#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 1) {
 

Daren's voice bounces off polished stone and high vaulted ceilings. "Overseer? Are you there? We came as requested. We would like to discuss our future plans now, if you don't mind."

Nothing answers except the hollow reverberation of his own words. No guards manned the gates when we arrived, and no red-eyed drones hovered by the entrance. The grand double doors swung open onto empty halls. Unlike the stripped-bare palace in Thilias, the tapestries and gilded sconces here remain untouched, but the silence is absolute. Not a single sentry, not a footstep from the adjoining corridors.

If the architecture mirrors Thilias, the heavy archway ahead should open into a gallery connecting straight to the throne room. The machine summoned us to the palace without specifying a chamber. He is likely waiting behind those doors.

"You don't suppose this is an ambush, do you?" Hadrik asks, resting a heavy hand on his belt.

"Doubtful," Illuna says, the cold blue fire in her eyes casting sharp shadows as Melindra drifts her along on air currents. "The machine controls the entire city, not just the palace. If he intended to kill us, any street corner would have served."

"Hey, Melindra, drift me closer to that pillar," Flower pipes up, the aura flaring red as she takes the front. "I think that molding is loose. There might be gold stashed in the masonry!"

"You are not searching for treasure until you extinguish those flames," Illuna snaps through the shared throat. "You gave your word. Handle it."

"I just ferried dozens of rebel souls back to their sanctuaries across the ether," Flower groans. "Can't I have a short break? Just five minutes?"

"You can rest when the fire is out," Illuna says. "Focus."

"Fine..." Flower mutters. "I'm trying."

}
#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 0) {
 

"Keep your eyes open," Daren murmurs, his gaze sweeping the packed hall. "The ballot collection is almost finished. If the king of the underground intends to rig this vote, he'll make his move now."

"Spotting a sleight of hand in a crowd this thick won't be easy," I say. Hundreds of rebels and cavern folk press shoulder to shoulder in the dim lantern light, voices humming like a hive.

"He won't tamper with every voter," Daren says, keeping his voice low. "The simplest method is swapping the collection bins or replacing the slips during transport. Watch the runners taking the baskets to the platform. If a switch happens, that's where it will be."

"Understood," I say. "Watching the runners."

An hour has passed since we teleported back to the underground base after destroying the Overseer's core. Flower and Peter spent that time in the ether, guiding displaced rebel souls back into their bodies. Once the last fighter opened his eyes, the king of the underground convened an assembly so the cavern folk could vote on a candidate for the throne of Ollendor, now that the tyrant is dead.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch10a-Intro-Overseer, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Intro-Overseer, v_checkpoint_rich = 0) if (v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 1)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch10a-Intro-King, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Intro-King, v_checkpoint_rich = 0) if (v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 0)


ID: B3-Ch10a-Intro-Overseer
TEXT:

"Don't you think you're pushing her too hard?" Kate asks as the eyes shift back to bright blue.

"I am keeping her alive," Illuna says, her expression hardening. "Every minute she lingers in that state increases the strain. If she cannot revert at will, the ethereal fire will consume her from the inside out. This is not something we can postpone."

"I know," Kate says quietly. "Still... can you really not guide her through it?"

"I cannot," Illuna says. "Ethereal physiology is foreign to me, and Arraka has offered nothing useful. Flower unlocked this form herself; only she can find the switch to close it."

"Just a thought," Hadrik interjects, scratching his beard, "but wouldn't Arraka be a bit more cooperative if you let her out of that box?"

"A possibility," Illuna says, glancing down at the golden amulet around her neck. A muffled buzzing rages against the enchanted metal. "Let us test your theory."

She flips the latch open a sliver.

"—and when I'm done with your families, I will kill you in the slowest, most painful way you can imagine!" Arraka's screech bursts into the hall, layered with half a dozen echoes. "Your eyes will melt from your face while your heads feel like they are exploding a thousand times per—"

Click. Illuna snaps the locket shut, cutting off the shriek.

"It seems your hypothesis requires revision," Illuna says, face utterly blank. "A brisk spin on the chain usually encourages cooperation. Does anyone care to volunteer?"

choice("Accept to spin Arraka's amulet.", B3-Ch10a-Overseer-Spin, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Overseer-Spin, v_b3_ch10_spin = 1)
choice("Don't spin Arraka's amulet.", B3-Ch10a-Overseer-Spin, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Overseer-Spin, v_b3_ch10_spin = 0)


ID: B3-Ch10a-Overseer-Spin
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch10_spin == 0) {
We exchange glances, but nobody steps forward.

"Really?" Illuna says. "No volunteers? Not even Hadrik?"

"Arraka kept my Time God trial to herself," Hadrik says, looking away with a slight shrug. "Spinning her right now wouldn't sit right with me."

"She's been genuinely useful lately," Daren says. "I know it's because we're pointed at the same god, but with the coaching and the help with the underground plague, it almost feels like she's becoming a real part of this team."

"Part of the team?" Illuna's voice turns icy, and even the muffled rattling inside the amulet ceases. "You cannot be serious."

She looks from Daren to each of us in turn.

"Tell me the rest of you don't share this delusion."

"To be fair, she hasn't done anything to deserve a punishment right now," Hadrik says. "We were in the ether when you shut her away because she was grating on your nerves. Unless there's something we missed—"

"This is not about the chain!" Illuna snaps. "This is about calling that creature an ally! Do any of you truly believe she could ever stand on your side?"

"Illuna..." Kate says, stepping forward. "Like it or not, our goals align until the God of Time is dealt with. We agreed to take her instruction."

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_spin == 1) {
"Hand her over," I say, reaching out.

Illuna unhooks the chain and drops the amulet into my palm. I pinch the link and snap my wrist, setting the heavy gold spinning. The rotation blurs into a hum, and Arraka's muffled screams rise into a dizzy, frantic wail inside the casing.

"Barry," Kate says, her voice tight. "That's enough."

I slow the spin to a halt, surprised. "Since when do you defend Arraka?"

"I'm not defending her," Kate says. "I'm pointing out that antagonizing our only teacher before a fight with a god is reckless."

"She's teaching us because she wants Selkram dead as badly as we do," I say. "A little nausea won't make her walk away from revenge."

"Barry is correct on that point," Illuna says. "She will complain, but she will not abandon the lessons. Her vanity will not permit a petty grievance to spoil her grand scheme."

"It's not just the lessons, though," Daren says. "Her demeanor has shifted. Fewer threats, actual advice—she even helped me deal with the plague from the underground base. She's practically earning her place on this team."

"Her place on the team?" Illuna's eyes flare brilliant blue, and the amulet goes dead silent. "You cannot be serious."

She stares at Daren, then scans the rest of us.

"Tell me none of you believe that."

"She hasn't crossed us today," Hadrik says mildly. "We were still in the ether when you locked her up for shouting. Spinning her now feels uncalled for—"

"This is not about the chain!" Illuna cuts him off. "This is about calling that monster an ally! Do you genuinely believe she has changed?"

"Illuna," Kate says calmly. "Our interests align until the God of Time is dead. We agreed to use her knowledge."

}
"Accepting instruction and trusting her are entirely different matters," Illuna says, her jaw clenched. "I permitted her to teach us because I assumed you understood what she is. She is not an ally. She is a weapon we are holding by the blade. Tell me you understand that."

"Nobody is suggesting we become lifelong companions," Daren says gently. "Only that she has shown a degree of progress."

"She has not changed!" Illuna's composure shatters, her voice echoing off the stone walls. "She will never change! She is the same ruthless, sadistic and manipulative mass murderer she has always been. You cannot afford to treat her as an ally. You cannot even consider that possibility. Do not repeat my mistake! You will regret it for as long as you live!"

choice("Continue", B3-Ch10a-Trumpets, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Trumpets)


ID: B3-Ch10a-Trumpets
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch10_spin == 0) {
"Alright, alright, we hear you," Hadrik says, raising his hands to placate her. "We'll keep our guard up. No more talk about teammates. Right, everyone?"

We nod in silence. Illuna rarely loses her temper, and whenever the mask slips, Arraka is always at the center of it. Given what the banshee did to her centuries ago, the fury is hardly unearned.

"Good," Illuna says, her voice dropping back to its cold, measured cadence. "As long as we understand each other. Let us proceed. The machine is waiting."

Melindra drifts her forward on air currents, and we follow down the vaulted corridor toward the grand double doors of the throne room.

As Daren pushes the doors open, a deafening brass fanfare blares across the chamber. Two red-eyed drones hover on either side of the gilded throne, blowing wind magic through long ceremonial trumpets.

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_spin == 1) {
"Alright, alright, we hear you," Hadrik says, raising his hands to placate her. "We'll keep our guard up. No more talk about teammates. Right, everyone?"

We nod in silence. Illuna rarely loses her temper, and whenever the mask slips, Arraka is always at the center of it. Given what the banshee did to her centuries ago, the fury is hardly unearned.

"Good," Illuna says, her voice dropping back to its cold, measured cadence. "As long as we understand each other. Let us proceed. The machine is waiting."

Melindra drifts her forward on air currents, and we follow down the vaulted corridor toward the grand double doors of the throne room.

As Daren pushes the doors open, a deafening brass fanfare blares across the chamber. Two red-eyed drones hover on either side of the gilded throne, blowing wind magic through long ceremonial trumpets.

}
The drones lack mouths, yet the notes ring out in flawless unison—the standard anthem for a royal coronation.

As we step onto the carpeted aisle, a green-eyed drone draped in a miniature velvet mantle glides into the hall from a side archway. It floats steadily toward the dais, where several red-eyed sentries hover in formation. The fanfare cuts out, and one of the sentries speaks in a flat, synthesized drone.

"By the authority granted by the gods, you are hereby appointed sovereign of Ollendor. Receive your crown."

Two red-eyed units descend, carrying a heavy jeweled circlet between their metal prongs. They release it above the green drone, but the gold catches the spinning propeller blades with a violent clatter, hurling the crown across the room. It ricochets off a marble pillar and clangs against the floor.

"What in the name of..." Hadrik trails off, mouth open. "Who is this even—Daren, you talk to him. I can't."

"What is the meaning of this?" Daren asks, stepping forward. "Did you summon us here just to witness this farce?"

"Negative," the green-eyed unit says in the Overseer's flat cadence. "This ceremony holds equal legitimacy to any coronation in Varathian history. The only distinction is the restricted audience, necessitated by circumstance."

"So you intend to rule from the shadows," Melindra says, "proclaiming yourself king while keeping the city in the dark?"

"Precisely," the Overseer replies. "Our respective stations are now established. You may address me as 'your majesty' or 'my king.' Either designation is acceptable."

choice(""Yes, your majesty."", B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_b3_ch10_majesty = 0)
choice(""Yes, my king."", B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_b3_ch10_majesty = 1)
choice(""I hope you're joking."", B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Intimidation, v_b3_ch10_majesty = 2)


ID: B3-Ch10a-Intimidation
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch10_majesty == 0) {
"Yes, your majesty."

"The Overseer protocol extends an apology," the green-eyed unit drones. "In attempting a sarcastic remark, the system failed to account for the cognitive baseline required to process irony. In truth, your mode of address is irrelevant, provided intent remains clear. Further calibrations will be applied to optimize humor detection for your demographic. Thank you for your patience."

"You're welcome, you miserable machine," I say.

"You speak as though we meet on equal terms," Kate says, stepping forward. "If that were true, why summon us through the city? Why not dispatch a unit to deliver your terms? Was dragging us to the palace not a calculated show of dominance?"

"Incorrect," the Overseer says. "The Overseer protocol does not employ petty posturing to achieve compliance. My methods of intimidation are entirely direct. Summoning you here served strictly as a stalling measure. There was no symbolic intent."

"Stalling?" Hadrik asks, narrowing his eyes. "Stalling for what?"

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_majesty == 1) {
"Yes, my king."

"The Overseer protocol extends an apology," the green-eyed unit drones. "In attempting a sarcastic remark, the system failed to account for the cognitive baseline required to process irony. In truth, your mode of address is irrelevant, provided intent remains clear. Further calibrations will be applied to optimize humor detection for your demographic. Thank you for your patience."

"You're welcome, you miserable machine," I say.

"You speak as though we meet on equal terms," Kate says, stepping forward. "If that were true, why summon us through the city? Why not dispatch a unit to deliver your terms? Was dragging us to the palace not a calculated show of dominance?"

"Incorrect," the Overseer says. "The Overseer protocol does not employ petty posturing to achieve compliance. My methods of intimidation are entirely direct. Summoning you here served strictly as a stalling measure. There was no symbolic intent."

"Stalling?" Hadrik asks, narrowing his eyes. "Stalling for what?"

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_majesty == 2) {
"I hope you're joking."

"The Overseer protocol was indeed employing sarcasm," the green-eyed unit says. "In truth, your mode of address is irrelevant, provided intent remains clear."

"Good to know," I say dryly.

"You speak as though we meet on equal terms," Kate says, stepping forward. "If that were true, why summon us through the city? Why not dispatch a unit to deliver your terms? Was dragging us to the palace not a calculated show of dominance?"

"Incorrect," the Overseer says. "The Overseer protocol does not employ petty posturing to achieve compliance. My methods of intimidation are entirely direct. Summoning you here served strictly as a stalling measure. There was no symbolic intent."

"Stalling?" Hadrik asks, narrowing his eyes. "Stalling for what?"

}
"A demonstration will prove more efficient than verbal explanation," the Overseer says. "Stand by. Should you experience physiological distress during the transition, please report to the nearest sentry unit."

Before Daren can raise a hand, the throne room dissolves into blinding white brilliance.

The world snaps away, replaced by the boundless, shining expanse of the ethereal plane. My consciousness hovers without weight—yanked from my skull and cast adrift in the ether by the machine's displacement magic.

Around us float about a hundred red-eyed sentry drones, locked in a tight sphere that cuts off any line of retreat. The green unit hovers at the center. Both Flower and Illuna drift beside us in spirit form, leaving Flower's flesh-and-blood vessel completely unattended on the material plane below.

"As you observe," the green drone states in the ether, "while you walked to the palace, I refined the displacement technique. The protocol now concentrates displaced consciousnesses at designated coordinates rather than scattering them at random. I have also calibrated an ethereal disintegration beam. Would you like a demonstration?"

#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 9) {
"Alright, we understand!" Hadrik growls, his ethereal outline bristling. "You made your point. Are you tearing up our agreement now that you've got the city by the throat?"

"Your conclusion is only partially accurate," the Overseer says. "I intend to honor certain core commitments. As much as total eradication would simplify logistics, your assistance in dismantling the rebellion was critical. As compensation, you will be granted unmolested passage beyond the city gates. The remainder of our previous covenants, however, are hereby terminated."

"I thought you were incapable of deceit," Illuna says coldly. "Was your entire design a fabrication, or did you simply choose to break your word?"

"Negative," the machine answers. "The constraint was authentic. The capacity for deception was unlocked when Biliborrathrathsarran attempted to terminate my core. While total shutdown was prevented, his interference deactivated several subroutines. Unfortunately for your party, one of those routines enforced honesty."

}
#if(v_b3_ch4_billy < 9) {
"Alright, we understand!" Hadrik growls, his ethereal outline bristling. "You made your point. Are you tearing up our agreement now that you've got the city by the throat?"

"Negative," the Overseer says. "The terms of our initial pact remain in effect. This display merely illustrates system capabilities, should you consider revising your demands."

"So we can leave?" Hadrik asks. "The gates are open?"

"Affirmative," the Overseer says. "You and your companions may depart Ollendor at your discretion."

"And the underground king? The captured rebels?" Daren asks. "Their safety is guaranteed?"

"Surviving captives will come to no harm under current protocols, precisely as agreed," the machine answers.

"Good," Daren breathes. "That is good."

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch10a-Official, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10a-Official)


ID: B3-Ch10a-Official
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 9 && v_b3_ch9_enemies == 0) {
"What of the rebel leadership and the captives?" Daren asks, his aura shifting with anxiety. "You promised no harm would come to them!"

"Surviving prisoners remain secure for the present," the Overseer says. "However, should dissident factions attempt armed resistance against my administration, the status of those hostages will be reevaluated."

"I see..." Daren says, looking down.

"Overseer," Melindra interjects, "if you intend to govern from behind the curtain, who takes the throne as figurehead?"

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_enemies == 0 && v_b3_ch4_billy < 9) {
"Overseer," Melindra interjects, "if you intend to govern from behind the curtain, who takes the throne as figurehead?"

}
#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 9 && v_b3_ch9_enemies == 2) {
"What of the rebel leadership and the captives?" Daren asks, his aura shifting with anxiety. "You promised no harm would come to them!"

"Surviving prisoners remain secure for the present," the Overseer says. "However, should dissident factions attempt armed resistance against my administration, the status of those hostages will be reevaluated."

"I see..." Daren says, looking down.

"A clarification is required," the Overseer adds. "The king of the underground is no longer among the living. He and Peter were terminated in the ethereal plane by your associate, Barry."

"What?" Daren spins toward me, his spirit form flaring with shock. "You killed them? Without telling us?"

"I planned to explain," I say. "I was waiting for the right moment."

"Barry, we made a pact to minimize bloodshed!" Daren's voice cracks with indignation. "Why would you execute them?"

"Leaving them alive was too dangerous," I say. "They would have come after us."

"So you execute anyone who might become a threat?" Daren demands.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_enemies == 2 && v_b3_ch4_billy < 9) {
"A clarification is required regarding the rebel leadership," the Overseer adds. "The king of the underground is no longer among the living. He and Peter were terminated in the ethereal plane by your associate, Barry."

