ID: B3-Ch10a-Prisoners
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch10_wrong == 0 && v_b3_ch8_king == 5) {
"You may be right."

"I don't buy a syllable of it," Hadrik snorts. "He sent Albert to slit our throats, realized we were too tough to chew, and cooked up this story after the fact."

"Perhaps," Daren says. "We may never know for certain."

"Whether he plotted murder is irrelevant," Kate says, her arms crossed. "What matters is what happens to the captives in the towers."

"We can ask Kelrim directly," Daren says, gesturing toward the aisle. "Here he comes."

Kelrim approaches with Sir Horace trailing half a step behind.

"Congratulations, Kelrim!" Daren greets him with a broad smile. "A well-earned victory."

"I still cannot grasp it..." Kelrim murmurs, wide-eyed. "To think so many placed their faith in me. Thank you for your counsel. I could not have stood on that stage without you."

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_wrong == 1 && v_b3_ch8_king == 5) {
