ID: B3-Ch10a-Interesting
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch10_third,1) if (v_b3_ch10_puzzle == 1)
achievement("Third piece of the puzzle",v_ac_b3_ch10_third)
#if(v_b3_ch10_puzzle == 1) {
"They wind down shortly," Melindra says. "The moment the blades retract, I'll throw the true release lever, we grab the fragments, and we sprint for daylight."

"We can still collect the pieces?" Kate asks.

"If we move fast," Melindra says. "The mechanism is resetting. Drop the barriers."

"Are you certain?" Kate asks.

"Drop them!" Melindra insists. "Before the reset window closes."

Kate dismisses the ice walls.

"Pulling now," Melindra calls, throwing the correct handle on the opposite wall. "Go!"

A stone block slides into the wall, revealing an ancient brass receptacle with an iron button. Flower smacks the switch, catching the dislodged stone fragment as it pops free. I hit the button right behind her, pocket my own puzzle piece, and we scramble back to the group.

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_puzzle == 0) {
"They wind down shortly," Melindra says. "The moment the blades retract, I'll throw the true release lever, we grab the fragment, and we sprint for daylight."

"We can still collect the piece?" Kate asks.

"If we move fast," Melindra says. "The mechanism is resetting. Drop the barriers."

"Are you certain?" Kate asks.

"Drop them!" Melindra insists. "Before the reset window closes."

Kate dismisses the ice walls.

"Pulling now," Melindra calls, throwing the correct handle on the opposite wall. "Go!"

A stone block slides into the wall, revealing an ancient brass receptacle with an iron button. Flower smacks the switch, catching the dislodged stone fragment as it pops free. She stows it in her pocket, and we scramble back to the group.

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_spin == 1) {
"Up the stairs!" Melindra commands. "Before the secondary traps prime!"

"After you," Illuna says.

"Move!"

We take the steps three at a time, bursting into the upper house and slamming the stone hatch shut. An echoing blast rumbles through the foundations below as the entire lower level resets its defense grid.

"We made it!" Melindra exhales, wiping dust from her brow. "And we got the prize. Told you I knew the way."

"That was reckless," Illuna says coldly. "A hair's breadth from catastrophe."

"I didn't invite an assassin!" Melindra shoots back. "How did he track us anyway?"

"An excellent inquiry," Illuna says, unlatching the amulet at her throat. "Care to enlighten us, Arraka?"

"Delighted," Arraka's voice purrs from the metal. "He spotted you gliding across the skyline, boarded a military carriage, veiled the engine with silence and invisibility, and trailed you here."

"You knew from the start?" Illuna demands.

"I might have mentioned it," Arraka sneers, "if someone hadn't sent me spinning like a carnival top."

"You made your point," Illuna says, leaving the latch cracked. "Fail us again, and the chain returns."

"Whatever," Arraka snorts.

"Flower, revert to your base form," Illuna instructs. "Long-range ethereal travel is finished for today."

"Right," Flower says, red eyes dimming slightly. "Let me teleport to our sanctuary and shut it down."

}
