ID: B3-Ch10a-Section-Ending
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 0) {
Once everyone is packed, we march to the teleporter chamber, exchanging parting words with the rebel guards along the route. At the platform, we ask the technician to hold the sequence while we bid Leila farewell one by one.

Though we aimed to be brief, each goodbye lingers. Daren presents Leila with an enchanted transceiver, instructing her to deliver it to Dr. Reidzek so we can maintain contact from the road.

When Kate steps forward, her composure shatters. Tears spill over her cheeks as she pulls Leila into a fierce embrace.

"I'll miss you so much," Kate chokes out, squeezing her tight. "I promise I'll return. I'll bring Diane, and Barry, and everyone else, and we'll—"

}
#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 1) {
Once everyone is packed, we leave the inn together and gather in the morning street to bid Leila farewell one by one.

Though we aimed to be brief, each goodbye lingers. Daren presents Leila with an enchanted transceiver, instructing her to deliver it to Dr. Reidzek so we can maintain contact from the road.

When Kate steps forward, her composure shatters. Tears spill over her cheeks as she pulls Leila into a fierce embrace.

"I'll miss you so much," Kate chokes out, squeezing her tight. "I promise I'll return. I'll bring Diane, and Barry, and everyone else, and we'll—"

}
"What is wrong with you people?" Arraka's voice erupts from the amulet. "You will see each other in a week, yet you weep like schoolchildren! Is there no ceiling to your foolishness?"

"How do you know it's only a week?" Daren asks, frowning at the locket. "The tournament could continue for months—"

"I am not speaking of your wretched tournament, you dullard!" Arraka snarls. "I am speaking of Selkram's ritual! Did you forget he adjourned the second trial to summon us again? We will all be pulled into his domain together, whether you like it or not!"

"Leila won't be traveling with us," Hadrik points out. "How does he draw her in from afar?"

#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 0) {
"Do you believe distance hinders a god?" Arraka mocks. "If the mute girl is not standing beside you, he will pluck her from her bed. If Eiden can track a soul across the continent, the God of Time can certainly drag her to his altar. Selkram never permits a participant to escape his trials. You will see your precious Leila within ten days at most. Now cease your sniveling! I am trying to focus!"

"Well..." Kate wipes her cheeks with the back of her sleeve, sniffing. "In that case... see you soon?"

"See you soon," Leila writes with a radiant smile.

We give the technician the signal, the magic flares, and we vanish from the caverns in a burst of light.

}
#if(v_b3_ch8_overseer2 == 1) {
"Do you believe distance hinders a god?" Arraka mocks. "If the mute girl is not standing beside you, he will pluck her from her bed. If Eiden can track a soul across the continent, the God of Time can certainly drag her to his altar. Selkram never permits a participant to escape his trials. You will see your precious Leila within ten days at most. Now cease your sniveling! I am trying to focus!"

"Well..." Kate wipes her cheeks with the back of her sleeve, sniffing. "In that case... see you soon?"

"See you soon," Leila writes with a radiant smile.

We turn toward Ollendor's northern gates, waving one last goodbye as we take to the open road.

}
choice("Proceed to next section of chapter", B3-Ch10b-Preoccupied, v_current_scene = B3-Ch10b-Preoccupied)
